{
  "title": "91: al-Shams الشمس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالشَّمْسِ وَضُحٰٮهَاۙ‏(1)\nWASH SHAMSE WA ZOHAAHAA.\nBy the sun and his radiation!\nوَالْقَمَرِ اِذَا تَلٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(2)\nWAL QAMARE EZAA TALAAHAA.\nBy the moon when she followeth after it!\nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا جَلّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(3)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA JALLAAHAA.\nBy the Day when it unfoldeth its light!\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰٮهَا ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAAHAA.\nBy the Night when it enshroudeth it!\nوَالسَّمَآءِ وَمَا بَنٰٮهَا ۙ‏(5)\nWAS SAMAAA-E WA MAA BANAAHAA.\nBy the heaven as it is built!\nوَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا طَحٰٮهَا ۙ‏(6)\nWAL ARZE WA MAA TAHAAHAA.\nBy the earth as it is expanded forth!\nوَنَفْسٍ وَّمَا سَوّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(7)\nWA NAFSINW WA MAA SAWWAAHAA.\nBy the soul as it is perfected!\nفَاَلْهَمَهَا فُجُوْرَهَا وَتَقْوٰٮهَا ۙ‏(8)\nFA-ALHAMAHAA FOJOORAHAA WA TAQWAAHAA.\nAnd inspired unto it (against) its vices and (about) its piety!\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ مَنْ زَكّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(9)\nQAD AFLAHA MAN ZAKKAAHAA.\nIndeed, succeedeth he who purifieth it!\nوَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ دَسّٰٮهَا ؕ‏(10)\nWA QAD KHAABA MAN DASSAAHAA.\nAnd indeed, faileth he who polluted it!\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِطَغْوٰٮهَآ  ۙ‏(11)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO BE-TAGHWAAHAA.\nBelied (the truth the Tribe), Thamood, due to their rebellious impiety!\nاِذِ انْۢبَعَثَ اَشْقٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(12)\nEZIM BA-A’SA ASHQAAHAA.\nWhen rose up the worst wretch among them (with mischief)!\nفَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ نَاقَةَ اللّٰهِ وَسُقْيٰهَا ؕ‏(13)\nFAQAALA LAHUM RASOOLUL LAAHE NAAQATAL LAAHE WA SUQYAAHAA.\nThen said unto them (Saleh) the Apostle of God: ‘‘It is the She Camel of God, (leave her) and its drink!\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَعَقَرُوْهَا  ۙفَدَمْدَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِذَنْۢبِهِمْ فَسَوّٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(14)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-A’QAROOHAA, FA-DAMDAMA A’LAYHIM RABBOHUM BE-ZAMBEHIM FASAWWAAHAA.\nBut they belied him and hamstrung her, so crushed them their Lord for their sins, and levelled them (all with the ground)\nوَلَا يَخَافُ عُقْبٰهَا‏(15)\nWA LAA YAKHAAFO UQBAAHAA.\nAnd He feareth not (any one against) the consequences (they met)",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah and has 15 verse. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (S) that the reward for reciting this Surah is compared to the things upon which the sun and the moon shine.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the person who recites Surah as-Shams, al-Layl, az-Zoha and al-Insherah will, on the Day of Judgement, find all creatures of the earth testifying on his behalf and Allah will accept their testimony and give him a place in Jannah. Recitation of this Surah also leads to an increase in sustenance, courage and popularity amongst the people."
